_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 41
---
order: 41
---
short_label: X.41
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on them medial and the rectangle contained by them medial and also incommensurable with the sum of the squares on them are added together, then the whole straight line is irrational; let it be called the <i>side of the sum of two medial areas.</i>
----
proof:

Let two straight lines {AB} and {BC} incommensurable in square and satisfying the given conditions be added together. [!just X.35]

I say that {AC} is irrational.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="210" height="350" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.41 diagram" src="propX41.gif"/></noscript>
